<section style="padding:96px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Torbay sits on the northeast Avalon coast just north of St. John's, and a lot of the homes here keep their heating oil tank outside where it takes the full brunt of the North Atlantic. Salt air, sideways rain and a winter of freeze and thaw are hard on steel, and a tank that looked fine at the fall fill can be weeping at a seam by February. Harbour Tank Co replaces and removes residential oil tanks across Torbay, from the older homes around the Bight and along Torbay Road to the newer builds on bigger lots out toward Indian Meal Line and Bauline Line.</p><p>We handle the whole job: the new tank, the tag, the old tank hauled away, and the paperwork your oil supplier needs before they'll deliver again. Estimates are free and in writing, and we're licensed and insured. If your tag has already expired and a driver has turned around in your driveway, call <strong>(709) 800-3117</strong> any hour and we'll get you sorted.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Torbay</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Torbay Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Oil Tank Replacement in Torbay</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">New steel or fibreglass heating oil tanks installed, tagged and registered for Torbay homes, with the old tank taken away on our truck. We set every tank on a solid, level base so it stays put through the frost.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Oil Tank Removal</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Switched to a heat pump, or selling a house with a tank that's past its date? We drain, disconnect and remove the old tank from your Torbay property and leave you with a record that it's gone.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Fibreglass Tank Upgrades</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Fibreglass doesn't rust, which matters when your tank faces the wind off the Bight. A longer tag life means fewer replacements and fewer refused deliveries down the road.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #D9E6E6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(13,44,71,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Open Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#0E4F5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Expired Tag and Leak Emergencies</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Refused delivery on a cold night, or smell oil near the tank? Our 24/7 emergency line exists for exactly that, and Torbay is a short run up Torbay Road from St. John's.</p>
      </div>
</div>
